
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
+ sorted-pairs [U64]
    - pairs [U64]

` The pairs in order, each a place in one list above a place in another: sorted by the low word,
` then, keeping that order, by the high word, each by counting how many take each place. So the
` work is as large as the pairs are many and the places they name.
ordered-by(ordered-by(pairs, 0), 32)

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ do ordered-by [U64]
    - pairs [U64]
    - shift U64

. top Size = 0
for pair in pairs
    . place = word-of(pair, shift)
    if place > top
        top = place
. starts [Size]
for _ in 0 .. < top + 2
    starts += 0
for pair in pairs
    starts[word-of(pair, shift) + 1] += 1
for position in 1 .. < starts.length
    starts[position] += starts[position - 1]
. ordered [U64]
for _ in 0 .. < pairs.length
    ordered += 0
for pair in pairs
    . place = word-of(pair, shift)
    ordered[starts[place]] = pair
    starts[place] += 1
= ordered

━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
_ word-of Size
    - pair U64
    - shift U64

((pair /rshift/ shift) /and/ 0xffffffff) as Size
